            <ArticleTitle>Congenital diaphragmatic hernia presenting as splenic rupture in an adult.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e9-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the case of a 66-year-old man with a congenital diaphragmatic hernia and splenic rupture. The adult presentation of congenital posterolateral diaphragmatic (Bochdalek) hernia is rare. We describe the operative approach and provide a brief review of the literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
